==Trivia==
*The [[Bats]] that the Night Witch spawns resemble the in-life bat species called "''Desmodus rotundus"'' ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_vampire_bat common vampire bat]). The common vampire bat is a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematophagy hematophagous] bat species that primarily feeds on the blood of livestock, which is done by biting their prey while they are sleeping. In Clash Royale, Bats attack in a similar way by biting their enemies.
*The Night Witch is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], Bats, [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], and [[Ice Wizard]].
**The Night Witch is confirmed to be [[Witch]]'s sister, according to the [https://youtu.be/p0KUcGDRJjc?t=46 Night Witch Karaoke Contest video] and her description in Clash of Clans.
**An opposing [[Star Points|Star Level 2 skin]] resembles the Level 13 Night Witch in Clash of Clans.
**The [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Witch Night Witch in Clash of Clans] is ranged and deals area damage, unlike in Clash Royale.
*The Night Witch is one of the first troop [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], Ram Rider, Miner, Royal Ghost, Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], and [[Fisherman]].
*In the Korean, Portuguese, Persian, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Night Witch's name translates to "Dark Witch". In the French and Finnish language settings of the game, the Night Witch's name translates to "Witch of the Night". In the Japanese and Thai language settings of the game, the Night Witch's name translates to "Dark Necromancer" and "Night Magic Girl" respectively.
*The Night Witch is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays her, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, P.E.K.K.A., Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], Goblin Giant, [[Golem]], Bowler, [[Electro Wizard]], Inferno Dragon, [[Sparky]], Lava Hound, [[Super Lava Hound]], and the [[Monk]].
*In [[Arenas|Spooky Town]], a Night Witch statue can be seen behind the enemy's [[King's Tower]].
*It is rumored that the [[Super Witch]] has been summoned from all the other 3 Witches, as demonstrated in the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VQf90EQVeX8 Super Witch trailer], hence explaining the combination of all the other Witches' abilities.
*The Night Witch is the only troop that has been featured with a [[Buff#Passive Heal|Passive Heal]] [[buff]].
*The Night Witch is featured as a [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Mortis?file=Mortis_Skin-Night_Witch.png character skin for Mortis] in Brawl Stars.
*The Night Witch, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, and Prince, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater].
*The Night Witch is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Night Witch is the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
***The Night Witch Rocking Emote may be a reference to [https://adventuretime.fandom.com/wiki/Marceline Marceline] from [https://adventuretime.fandom.com/wiki/Adventure_Time_Wiki Adventure Time], being a vampire girl that plays an electric guitar.
**The Night Witch is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Night Witch is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Dancing Witch decoration is created by Myoho.
***The Night Witch decoration's description says "''Bats frighten me. It's time my enemies share my dread!"'' which is a reference to a quote mentioned in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_Begins Batman Begins].
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Night Witch does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*In the Clash-A-Rama episode "[https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/%22Archer_Departure%22 Archer Departure]", the Night Witch was incorrectly shown as a [[:Category:5-Elixir Cards|5-Elixir]] card.
*On 27/3/2023, a [[Training Camp|Trainer]] was added to the game called Boss Cheddar, and used a Level 18 Night Witch in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], despite the highest Level being Level 14 at the time. This Trainer was removed on 18/4/2023.
*The initial balance change for Night Witch on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/6/2023)|6/6/2023 balance changes]] was the addition of 2 Bats after death, but it lowered to 1 Bat [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-48-balance-wip last minute].

